<h2>Indian groundnut kernels for export</h2>
<p>We supply HPS (Hand-Picked-Selected) groundnut kernels, shelled and sized to your count specification. This is, by dollar value, the largest single product line in our entire trade dataset — USD 823M in 2024 — and it is overwhelmingly a Southeast Asian story: Indonesia alone takes around 36% of total value, with Vietnam, the Philippines, Malaysia and Thailand rounding out a market base that together accounts for roughly 73% of exports.</p>

<p>We source from Gujarat's Saurashtra belt and Andhra Pradesh/Rajasthan, the two dominant groundnut-producing regions. Kernels are hand-sorted to remove damaged, discoloured or foreign material, graded by count-per-ounce, and packed to your specification.</p>

<h2>Groundnut kernel export policy</h2>
<p>Groundnut kernel export is Free under current Indian policy — there is no Minimum Export Price or comparable volatility here. Documentation requirements do vary by destination: EU-bound shipments need APEDA contract registration and aflatoxin testing, and Russia-bound shipments need pre-shipment quality certification from an approved lab. These are standard destination-market requirements we handle as part of order documentation, not a barrier to export.</p>

<h2>How should I specify groundnut kernels?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Count/oz.</strong> 38/42, 40/44, 50/60, 60/70 and other bands are available — smaller numbers mean larger kernels and typically a price premium.</li>
  <li><strong>Aflatoxin.</strong> Ask for testing if your destination market sets a specific limit — this is standard practice for EU-bound cargo especially.</li>
  <li><strong>Packing.</strong> Bags for most buyers; jumbo bags for large-volume oil-crushing or confectionery buyers.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which markets buy Indian groundnut kernels?</h2>
<p>Indonesia is the clear leader, followed by Vietnam, the Philippines, Malaysia and Thailand — a genuinely Southeast Asia-centred trade. The UAE, Russia, Algeria, Bangladesh and Iran take meaningful additional volume outside that core cluster.</p>

